As a (Senior) Manager, you will assume responsibility for, although not limited to, the following activities:

• Lead teams and deliver project work across a range of clients based either from our office in Amsterdam or at the client site;
• Capability in selling and delivering (large) program engagements;
• Mentoring and developing senior team members;
• Working closely with other Sia’ offices and leverage our global network to take part in cross-selling initiatives and widely share our knowledge;
• Track the latest developments, news and activities across the financial services industry and contribute to the development of the Sia brand in the Dutch market (publication of articles, blogs, networking);

As part of a diverse and motivated team, you will be involved in a range of projects with our clients, covering topics such as:

• Business strategy definition & implementation: elaboration of a business plan, digital strategy, market studies, financial modeling, benchmarks, data analysis;
• Business improvement: business processes study, mapping & reengineering, performance management design & implementation, benchmarks & analysis;
• Regulatory/Operational Risk transformation: analysis of the impacts of regulation, organization & processes compliance;
• Innovation: discovery and validation of emerging business opportunities, managing the development of prototypes, development of the market entry plan;
• Project management: management of business projects with both internal stakeholders and third parties.

• You have completed your Master’s Degree.
• You have at least 10 years of experience in management consulting and a good track record.
• English & Dutch speaker with excellent communication and presentation skills.
• You have a strong network within the Dutch banking or insurance market.
• You are experienced in business development and sales of consulting services.
• You have a strong interest in data and AI-related topics, the ability to quickly build expertise in these areas, and you’re excited about helping our clients seize the opportunities they offer.
• Strong entrepreneurial drive; thrives on growth challenges with regard to client development and business development.

What do we offer?

• Competitive salary with great extra advantages: a work phone, a clear and structured yearly salary increase and bonuses.
• Flexible transport options that match your personal needs.
• Training plan to develop yourself as an expert in your discipline.
• You have the opportunity to work from home, the client or our inspiring office in Amsterdam.
• Working in an international environment creates opportunities to share knowledge and work together on international projects with colleagues all over the world.

We are unable to provide a work permit for this position

Non-Dutch speaker will not be accepted

